es","\u002Fen\u002Freleases","en\u002F5.releases",[273],{"title":274,"icon":12,"path":275,"stem":276,"children":277,"page":12},"Versions","\u002Fen\u002Freleases\u002Fversions","en\u002F5.releases\u002F1.versions",[278,282],{"title":279,"path":280,"stem":281},"v3.1.0","\u002Fen\u002Freleases\u002Fversions\u002Fv3-1-0","en\u002F5.releases\u002F1.versions\u002F1.v3-1-0",{"title":283,"path":284,"stem":285},"v3.0.0","\u002Fen\u002Freleases\u002Fversions\u002Fv3-0-0","en\u002F5.releases\u002F1.versions\u002F2.v3-0-0",{"id":287,"title":117,"body":288,"description":1216,"extension":1217,"links":1218,"meta":1223,"navigation":1224,"path":118,"seo":1225,"stem":119,"__hash__":1226},"docs_en\u002Fen\u002F3.components\u002F2.text\u002F2.input-number.md",{"type":289,"value":290,"toc":1191},"minimark",[291,299,304,309,332,336,387,391,425,428,564,589,611,615,627,630,649,653,669,672,675,682,685,689,696,699,703,706,722,725,729,736,739,743,757,760,764,777,780,784,791,794,798,802,827,830,906,911,915,952,956,993,1121,1165,1184,1188],[292,293,294,298],"p",{},[295,296,297],"code",{},"v-model: number | null",".",[300,301,303],"h2",{"id":302},"usage","Usage",[305,306,308],"h3",{"id":307},"decimal-places-and-thousands-separators","Decimal places and thousands separators",[292,310,311,314,315,318,319,322,323,314,326,328,329,331],{},[295,312,313],{},"decimal"," defaults to ",[295,316,317],{},"false",", allowing only integers; a positive integer sets the number of decimal places, and ",[295,320,321],{},"true"," allows any number. ",[295,324,325],{},"thousand-separator",[295,327,321],{},", showing thousands separators on blur; pass ",[295,330,317],{}," for numbers such as years or codes that should not have them.",[333,334],"component-example",{"name":335},"input-number-decimal",[337,338,339,354,367],"ul",{},[340,341,342,343,346,347,350,351,353],"li",{},"While typing, the sign, decimal point and trailing zeros are kept; incomplete input (such as just ",[295,344,345],{},"-",") binds ",[295,348,349],{},"null",". On blur, the value is rounded and padded according to ",[295,352,313],{},", and thousands separators are shown.",[340,355,356,357,359,360,362,363,366],{},"Non-numeric characters and decimals beyond the set places cannot be typed, and pasted text is reverted too. When ",[295,358,313],{}," is ",[295,361,317],{}," or ",[295,364,365],{},"0",", the decimal point cannot be typed.",[340,368,369,370,359,373,376,377,359,379,362,381,383,384,386],{},"On focus, the text switches to the editable form without separators. ",[295,371,372],{},"inputmode",[295,374,375],{},"numeric"," when ",[295,378,313],{},[295,380,317],{},[295,382,365],{},", and ",[295,385,313],{}," otherwise, so phones show the matching number keyboard.",[305,388,390],{"id":389},"step-buttons","Step buttons",[292,392,393,396,397,400,401,404,405,408,409,412,413,416,417,420,421,424],{},[295,394,395],{},"buttons"," shows increment and decrement buttons (off by default), ",[295,398,399],{},"step"," is the amount per step (",[295,402,403],{},"1"," by default), and ",[295,406,407],{},"min",", ",[295,410,411],{},"max"," limit stepping with the buttons and keys. ",[295,414,415],{},"orientation"," sets the button layout: ",[295,418,419],{},"horizontal"," (default) puts decrement on the left and increment on the right; ",[295,422,423],{},"vertical"," stacks both on the right.",[333,426],{"name":427},"input-number-step",[337,429,430,453,459,476,492,535,547,554],{},[340,431,432,436,437,439,440,408,442,408,444,446,447,449,450,452],{},[433,434,435],"strong",{},"Keyboard",": with ",[295,438,395],{},", or when any of ",[295,441,399],{},[295,443,407],{},[295,445,411],{}," is passed, ArrowUp \u002F ArrowDown steps once in the focused input, PageUp \u002F PageDown steps 10 times, and Home \u002F End jump to ",[295,448,407],{}," \u002F ",[295,451,411],{}," (when set). Without these settings the arrow keys behave as in a normal text input. The buttons are not in the Tab order and are labelled \"Increment\" and \"Decrement\" (following the locale).",[340,454,455,458],{},[433,456,457],{},"Press and hold",": holding a button for more than 0.4 seconds keeps stepping until a limit is reached or the button is released. Pressing a button does not move focus away from the input.",[340,460,461,464,465,467,468,470,471,473,474,298],{},[433,462,463],{},"Empty value",": when the value is ",[295,466,349],{},", both increment and decrement start at ",[295,469,407],{},", or at ",[295,472,365],{}," without ",[295,475,407],{},[340,477,478,481,482,485,486,489,490,298],{},[433,479,480],{},"No floating-point errors",": steps are computed in decimal, so repeatedly adding ",[295,483,484],{},"0.25"," never gives ",[295,487,488],{},"0.7500000001","; the result is rounded to the places allowed by ",[295,491,313],{},[340,493,494,501,502,504,505,507,508,510,511,513,514,516,517,519,520,522,523,525,526,528,529,531,532,534],{},[433,495,496,498,499],{},[295,497,399],{}," and ",[295,500,313],{},": when ",[295,503,399],{}," has more decimal places than ",[295,506,313],{}," allows (for example ",[295,509,484],{}," with ",[295,512,313],{}," set to ",[295,515,317],{},"), the step is rounded to what ",[295,518,313],{}," allows (at least one smallest unit, ",[295,521,403],{}," for ",[295,524,317],{},") with a console warning. A ",[295,527,399],{}," that is not a number above 0, or a ",[295,530,407],{}," greater than ",[295,533,411],{},", is also ignored with a warning.",[340,536,537,540,541,543,544,546],{},[433,538,539],{},"Limits",": the increment button is disabled when the value is at or above ",[295,542,411],{},", and the decrement button at or below ",[295,545,407],{},". Both are disabled while disabled, loading, in a skeleton or in a disabled form.",[340,548,549,550,553],{},"Each step triggers the ",[295,551,552],{},"UFormField"," input and change validation, just like typing.",[340,555,556,498,558,560,561,298],{},[295,557,395],{},[295,559,415],{}," can have site-wide defaults, for example to show the buttons across the project: ",[295,562,563],{},"shuoUi.components.inputNumber.buttons: true",[565,566,567,498,569,571,572,575,576,498,579,582,583,588],"warning",{},[295,568,407],{},[295,570,411],{}," only limit the buttons and keys. ",[433,573,574],{},"A typed value outside the range is not corrected","; the bound value stays as typed, and stepping from it moves back into the range. Keep validating the range in the schema with ",[295,577,578],{},"v.minValue",[295,580,581],{},"v.maxValue","; see ",[584,585,587],"a",{"href":586},"#with-form-validation","With form validation"," below.",[292,590,591,592,449,595,598,599,602,603,606,607,610],{},"In horizontal layout the decrement button takes the place of the left ",[295,593,594],{},"icon",[295,596,597],{},"leadingIcon"," (the ",[295,600,601],{},"#leading"," slot still follows the button); use ",[295,604,605],{},"orientation=\"vertical\""," when you need a left icon. The increment button sits to the right of the unit, the ",[295,608,609],{},"#trailing"," slot and the loading icon, and the padding on both sides follows their actual width, so the number and unit are never pushed out.",[305,612,614],{"id":613},"unit","Unit",[292,616,617,618,359,620,622,623,626],{},"When ",[295,619,613],{},[295,621,321],{},", \"NTD\" is shown (\"元\" in Traditional Chinese, switching with the locale). The text can be changed in ",[584,624,47],{"href":625},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fmessages#overridable-items","; passing a string shows that text. Units vary in length, so the right padding follows the unit's actual width and the number never overlaps the unit.",[333,628],{"name":629},"input-number-unit",[292,631,632,498,634,636,637,641,642,644,645,449,647,298],{},[295,633,613],{},[295,635,325],{}," can also have site-wide defaults; see ",[584,638,640],{"href":639},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fcomponent-defaults#configurable-props","Configurable props",". The site-wide ",[295,643,613],{}," only accepts ",[295,646,321],{},[295,648,317],{},[305,650,652],{"id":651},"variants","Variants",[292,654,655,656,408,659,498,662,665,666,298],{},"Uses the ",[295,657,658],{},"variant",[295,660,661],{},"color",[295,663,664],{},"highlight"," of ",[295,667,668],{},"UInput",[333,670],{"name":671},"input-number-variant",[305,673,674],{"id":594},"Icon",[292,676,655,677,665,679,681],{},[295,678,594],{},[295,680,668],{},", shown on the left alongside the unit.",[333,683],{"name":684},"input-number-icon",[305,686,688],{"id":687},"size-and-states","Size and states",[292,690,691,692,695],{},"While loading, the spinner sits to the right of the unit and the number and unit move left to make room. See ",[584,693,102],{"href":694},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Foverview\u002Fcommon"," for the behavior shared by all states.",[333,697],{"name":698},"input-number-states",[300,700,702],{"id":701},"examples","Examples",[305,704,587],{"id":705},"with-form-validation",[292,707,708,709,712,713,498,715,717,718,721],{},"Use ",[295,710,711],{},"requiredNumber"," for required fields and add ranges with ",[295,714,578],{},[295,716,581],{},"; use ",[295,719,720],{},"optionalNonNegativeNumber"," for optional non-negative numbers. What gets validated and submitted is a number, without separators.",[333,723],{"name":724},"input-number-validation",[305,726,728],{"id":727},"step-buttons-with-validation","Step buttons with validation",[292,730,731,498,733,735],{},[295,732,407],{},[295,734,411],{}," do not replace validation: the buttons in this example only stop at 0, and the schema checks the upper limit; stepping above 40 shows the error right away.",[333,737],{"name":738},"input-number-step-validation",[305,740,742],{"id":741},"centered-numbers","Centered numbers",[292,744,745,748,749,752,753,756],{},[295,746,747],{},"ui.base"," has a built-in ",[295,750,751],{},"text-right","; pass ",[295,754,755],{},"text-center"," to center the number, which suits short fields inside a sentence. With a unit or while loading, the right padding follows the trailing